    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.IntervalScalar.staticL: C:static-interaction",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Ledger:2079 and claims.yaml:11759 reproduce IntervalScalar.lean:323-325: '4*exp 1*R*h²*lam^(alpha−2) + 4*√(exp 1)*D/((2−alpha)*(3−alpha))*(h^(3−alpha)/lam)'. TeX:2623-2626 has exactly 4e and 4√e. This is an unrestricted scalar definition; manuscript applications supply positive h,λ and α<2."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.IntervalScalar.staticB: C:static-interaction",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Ledger:2080 and claims.yaml:11766 match IntervalScalar.lean:328: 'staticB A := 3*exp 1*A²'. TeX:2620 defines 'B_alpha=3e A_alpha²'. There are no additional hypotheses in the definition."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.IntervalScalar.staticX: C:static-interaction",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Ledger:2081 and claims.yaml:11773 match IntervalScalar.lean:331: 'staticB A * σ² * R * h^(4−alpha)'. TeX:2627 defines 'x=B_alpha σ² R_alpha h^(4−alpha)'. Parameters are correctly abstracted as real scalars."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.IntervalScalar.staticE: C:static-interaction",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Ledger:2082 and claims.yaml:11780 match IntervalScalar.lean:335-338: 'σ²*staticL + (lam*h)⁻¹²*(staticX²*exp((3−alpha)*staticX^(1/(3−alpha))))'. TeX:2620,2628-2630 has γ=3−α and precisely this expression. Positive manuscript λ,h justify the inverse-power notation."
