    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.IntervalScalar.summable_dyadic_rpow: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Ledger:2086 and claims.yaml:11808 match IntervalScalar.lean:463-464: '0<lam', '0<q' imply summability of ((1/2)^j/lam)^q. TeX:2712-2713 says the positive powers yield convergent geometric series. This standalone formulation is correctly marked auxiliary."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.IntervalScalar.block_term_le: C:static-interaction",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Ledger:2087 and claims.yaml:11815 match IntervalScalar.lean:480-488: 'alpha<2', 'R≥0', positive λ,T,q, 'q≤lam⁻¹', β>0 and 's²=q^(−alpha0)'. TeX:2699-2713 uses β>2 and the same three powers 1−α0, 2−α−α0, 2β−3. The exponential endpoint bound and all displayed constants agree; arbitrary D is harmless because its term is retained exactly."
