    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.IntervalScalar.independent_blocks_scalar: C:static-interaction",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Ledger:2089 and claims.yaml:11829 match IntervalScalar.lean:566-568: '∀j,0≤E j', '0≤m 0' and the recurrence for j<K. TeX:2719-2721 iterates e^(λh_j)(1+E_j) and uses '1+y≤e^y'. The abstract recurrence and final exponent accurately capture this scalar step."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.IntervalScalar.ralpha_nonneg: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Ledger:2090 and claims.yaml:11836 match IntervalScalar.lean:588-590: any measure μ and '0<alpha<2' give nonnegativity of the formula with '(μ(ball 0 1)).toReal'. TeX:1988,2747 defines the same R_alpha for Radon measures. The broader toReal sign lemma is correctly auxiliary, with no assertion of finite mass for arbitrary measures."
