    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.IntervalScalar.static_interaction_paper: E:static-interaction",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Ledger:2092 and claims.yaml:11850 match IntervalScalar.lean:614-634. Lean assumes locally finite μ,Γ on R³ and '0<alpha<2', with the R,D formulas; TeX:1981-1992 has the full covariance class. Its omitted clauses enter only through the disclosed hY0/hY/hodd/hborn/hmean, identical to TeX:2664-2679. The weaker model identification and unused local-finiteness hypotheses are recorded."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.IntervalScalar.static_block_series_paper: E:static-block-series",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Ledger:2093 and claims.yaml:11857 match IntervalScalar.lean:642-654: locally finite μ,Γ on R³, '0<alpha', '0<alpha0<1', 'alpha+alpha0<2', positive λ,T and the dyadic σ² identity. TeX:2638-2641 states precisely the resulting series convergence, with constants from1985-1992. No analytic input is assumed."
