    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.IntervalScalar.independent_static_blocks_paper: E:independent-static-blocks",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Ledger:2094 and claims.yaml:11864 match IntervalScalar.lean:665-676. Lean's supplied 'm(j+1)≤exp(lam*h j)*(1+staticE)*m j' is the per-block bound in TeX:2714-2720. Its exponent matches TeX:2647-2652 after the stated index shift. The carried λh_j≤1, local finiteness and unformalized operator extensions are disclosed."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.IntervalScalar.invV: L:inventory-product",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Ledger:2095 and claims.yaml:11871 match IntervalScalar.lean:688-690: 'i^(−β)+k⁻¹*i^(−(β−1))+k^(alpha−2)*i^(−(2−alpha0))'. TeX:2914-2917 specifies k≥1 and the same v_i for product indices i≥1. The unrestricted Lean definition merely extends the formula outside its manuscript use."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.IntervalScalar.invB: L:inventory-product",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Ledger:2096 and claims.yaml:11878 match IntervalScalar.lean:694-695: 'i^(−β*l)*(1+l*i/k)²/(l!)^(3−alpha)'. TeX:2914,2918 has k≥1 and l≥2, with identical formula. The definition is unrestricted, but invCoeff uses this branch only for l≥2."
