    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.IntervalScalar.invCoeff: E:inventory-product",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Ledger:2097 and claims.yaml:11885 match IntervalScalar.lean:699-700: 'if l=0 then 1 else if l=1 then invV else invB'. TeX:2922 gives '1+v_i z+sum_(l≥2)b_(i,l)z^l'. Thus the coefficient object, including the constant and singleton branches, agrees."
