      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Ledger:2101 and claims.yaml:11913 match IntervalScalar.lean:727: arbitrary p has 'splitEll p≤2'. TeX:3019-3020 says 'a higher color has at most two metric factors'. The unrestricted elementary helper is appropriately auxiliary."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.IntervalScalar.splitFactor_nonneg: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Ledger:2102 and claims.yaml:11920 match IntervalScalar.lean:731-734: '0<h', '0<lam', arbitrary α,σ,κ,p imply nonnegativity. TeX:3011-3016 uses positive lengths and λ=k/T>0. No separate labelled sign statement exists, so the auxiliary mapping is appropriate."
