    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.IntervalScalar.two_mul_add_one_le_three_pow: P:interval-coefficients",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Ledger:2108 and claims.yaml:11962 match IntervalScalar.lean:857: arbitrary natural k has '2*k+1≤3^k'. TeX:3414-3415 uses 'prod_i(2k_i+1)≤3^k' with nonnegative k_i summing to k. The per-color inequality is exactly the elementary split-count input."
